"Because bone is alive, it responds to how you treat it. When you run, jump, and play, the extra force tells your bones to grow thicker and stronger. Astronauts who spend months in space, where their bones carry almost no weight, lose bone and must exercise every day to slow the loss. Your bones reach their greatest strength by your late twenties, and much of it is built while you are still in school. So move every day, and eat foods with calcium, such as milk, tofu, small dried fish, and dark green vegetables. Then try this: count the bones in one of your hands.": "4c1380aa590d",
